<title>DENMARK: Danish Aug yr/yr consumer prices fall to 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish Aug yr/yr consumer prices fall to 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices rose 0.2 per cent in August from July and were 2.5 percent higher than in August 1995, the National Statistics Office said on Friday.</p>
<p>The CPI data was issued under new EU-harmonised calculation methods. Under the traditional Danish national formula the respective figures would have risen 0.2 percent month-on-month with a 2.4 percent increase year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    NEW EU FORMULA	   August 1996  July 1996  August 1995</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)     +0.2	  -0.2	   +0.2</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	+2.5	  +2.6	   +1.7</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	  104.7	  104.5	  102.1</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)     +0.2	   -0.2	  +0.2</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	+2.4	   +2.3	  +1.6</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	  199.9	  199.5	  195.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Average analyst expectations were for a 2.3 percent rise from August 1995 according to the national formula.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969650</p>
</text>
